# CTF05 first-inverse owner: source-only proposal

This package adds a direct public owner API and five focused unexecuted tests.
It does not activate a production cache call or add cache/state fields. Native
Construction.cc884 calls exponential before inverse887, then Gammas890. The
future actual production driver must preserve assembly -> CTF06 exponential ->
CTF05 inverse before any inverse cache ingress can be activated. A direct helper
test/call here is not a claim that this whole-method order already exists.

initialize_construction_ctf_first_inverse borrows the accepted real first-assembly
owner. It retains original ConstructionId and actual assembly context, requires
the same context ID and ordinal1 selected one-dimensional no-source route, and
calls the unchanged invert_selected_ctf_matrix exactly once on the same AMat,
actual source-produced IdenMatrix and rcmax. No new matrix or identity evaluator,
node placement, timestep/history derivation, retry route or Native answer is
introduced. The accepted pure helper owns its ordinary AMat1/AInv copies.

The returned ConstructionCtfFirstInverse Result separates a real first-assembly
prerequisite Err, an actual assembly unavailable branch, inconsistent identity,
non-first attempt, unsupported selected context and actual inverse shape error.
A reached result contains the unchanged context and actual inverse return owner.
No finite/singularity/pivot guard or fallback is added: zero and nonfinite source
arithmetic remain actual values, and no scientific PASS is inferred from them.
The incoming assembly buffers are immutable and remain separately owned.

Only two fresh parent declarations are proposed against genuine current CTF03
canonical sources. They must later be composed/rebased with accepted CTF04 module
declarations; no pending CTF04 source is silently assumed canonical. The pure05
module/tests remain byte-identical accepted d593. The accepted first-assembly
owner is a held dependency, not a claim that current production already has it.
Existing coefficient arrays, cache hash, initial owner and all current production
cache/state source bytes are unchanged by this proposal.

Five focused tests exercise readonly buffers/context without caller==initial dt,
distinct unavailable prerequisites, stale owner/later attempt/context rejection,
real identity shape rejection without reconstruction, and retained nonfinite
inverse arithmetic. They use the actual accepted pure assembler to make their
ordinary fixture and contain no Native output or production oracle answers.
They are transport/ownership regressions, not differential numerical proof.

Deferred production plan: once CTF06 has a genuine first-exponential owner and
the real driver invokes it on this same assembly before inverse, retain the
first inverse beside those actual ordered construction owners, expose a readonly
state vector, and preserve unavailable branches. Do not insert an inverse call
immediately after assembly ahead of exponential. Native later retry attempts
and final coefficient state remain unpaired until a real retry driver exists.

Root alone may apply/format/build/run after independent source review and actual
pre-output scope/input policy. There are no future SHAs, expected Native arrays,
new numerical profiles, gate/completion claims or new QA execution framework.
No target import, compiler, formatter, Cargo, engine, Git, canonical edit,
scientific/weather output or binary read occurs in this source preparation.

